 The pages under `docs/` are this repository's source of truth for people and coding agents. This page says which page
 owns each fact; read it before writing one.
+
+## Kinds
+
+- [Philosophy](philosophy.md) owns standing trade-offs that guide future proposals, rather than one past choice.
+  This explanation page has a lead and `Tenets`; each tenet says what it rules out and links decisions that apply it.
+- [Architecture](architecture.md) owns the current parts and how they connect. This explanation page has a lead,
+  `Parts` and `How they connect`; it links the decisions behind structural choices.
+- [Decisions](adrs/README.md) own the reasons for individual foundational choices: choices whose reversal changes
+  how the system is built, rather than a local implementation detail. These explanation pages use
+  `NNNN-<slug>.md` and contain a lead, `Context`, `Options`, `Decision` and `Consequences`, including why alternatives
+  lost and the choice won. A standing trade-off across decisions belongs in Philosophy.
+- [Features](features/README.md) own current member-visible behavior. These reference pages have a lead, sections
+  describing the behavior and links to the decisions that shaped it.
+- [Runbooks](runbooks/README.md) own operational procedures for a trigger. These how-to pages have a lead naming
+  the trigger and owner, `Before you begin`, `Steps` with expected results and `If it fails`.
+- [Glossary](glossary.md) owns shared names. Each entry defines a term and lists rejected synonyms under `Avoid`.
+
+Each fact has one owner; other pages link it. The guides for kinds with multiple pages list each page and its purpose.
